      "summary": "Witness provenance, digest validation, coverage gating, and uncertainty routing are covered. The validator’s additional full-claim-text match can downgrade structurally valid gap claims that should reach internal review.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/ClaimValidator.cs",
          "line": 87,
          "message": "The full-claim-text containment check adds a structural requirement beyond the clarification’s listed checks and can suppress review for a structurally valid gap claim. After validating the witness, digest, and typed value, route a MissingRequirement claim to internal review without requiring its entire text to appear verbatim in the quote.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "After validating the witness, digest, and typed value, Validate requires the entire claim text to appear verbatim in every witness quote. A claim that fails this extra check is downgraded, and FindingRouter sends downgraded claims to NoAction.",
            "failureScenario": "With complete coverage, a current witness quote says “Reserve approval is pending,” and the typed value is “Reserve approval.” A claim text such as “Review the reserve approval requirement” passes the clarification’s structural checks, but is downgraded because the full claim text is not in the quote. Routing creates no internal review task, though the clarification requires every structurally valid MissingRequirement claim to go to review."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
